Subject: also ignore the --incognito command line switch

Patch 0032 ("Remove Incognito mode in gooroom-browser") strips the UI entry
points: the keyboard shortcut and command, the app menu item, the bookmark
context menu, the extension detail view and the bookmark manager. What it never
covered is chrome/browser/ui/startup/, so `gooroom-browser --incognito` still
reached IncognitoModePrefs::ShouldLaunchIncognitoInternal() and opened a real
off-the-record session. The removal had a hole that only the command line could
walk through.

Measured on 153 (+grm5u3/u4) with the same file opened twice, once without the
switch and once with it: the visit is recorded in History in the first run and
missing in the second, i.e. the second run really is off the record. 152 behaves
the same way, so this is not a 153 regression but a gap that has been open since
the UI was removed.

Drop the switch inside the GOOROOM_BUILD guard, next to the other Incognito
removals. The assignment is kept separate from the initializer so that
`command_line` stays used and `forced_by_switch` stays assignable below.

Index: gooroom-browser-debian.git/chrome/browser/prefs/incognito_mode_prefs.cc
===================================================================
--- gooroom-browser-debian.git.orig/chrome/browser/prefs/incognito_mode_prefs.cc
+++ gooroom-browser-debian.git/chrome/browser/prefs/incognito_mode_prefs.cc
@@ -156,6 +156,15 @@
   // the parental controls check (which can be quite slow) can be avoided
   // most of the time.
   bool forced_by_switch = command_line.HasSwitch(switches::kIncognito);
+#if defined(GOOROOM_BUILD)
+  // Gooroom removes Incognito mode entirely (see 0032). The UI entry points are
+  // gone, but the --incognito command line switch still reached this function
+  // and opened a real OTR session, so the removal had a hole that only the
+  // command line could walk through. Drop the switch here as well.
+  // Assign instead of replacing the initializer so that `command_line` stays
+  // used and `forced_by_switch` stays assignable below.
+  forced_by_switch = false;
+#endif
   if (for_subsequent_browsers) {
     forced_by_switch =
         forced_by_switch &&
